{0 console}

Colours, tables, trees and progress rows for OCaml command-line tools.

[console] prints into the terminal's normal scrollback and, while work
runs, redraws only the progress rows of a {!Console.Display}.

Its widgets lay out text in a style and print with
{{:https://erratique.ch/software/fmt}Fmt}, in the colours and the
{!Console.Theme} of the formatter that prints them, or as plain text on a
pipe:

{@ocaml[
# let sizes =
    Console.Table.(
      view
        [
          column (Console.View.text "Package");
          column ~align:`Right (Console.View.text "Size");
        ]
        [
          [ Console.View.text "console"; Console.View.text "42 KiB" ];
          [ Console.View.text "console-eio"; Console.View.text "9 KiB" ];
        ]);;
val sizes : Console.View.t = <abstr>
# Fmt.pr "%a@." Console.View.pp sizes;;
╭─────────────┬────────╮
│ Package     │   Size │
├─────────────┼────────┤
│ console     │ 42 KiB │
│ console-eio │  9 KiB │
╰─────────────┴────────╯
- : unit = ()
]}

{1:manuals Manuals}

{ul
{- {{!page-widgets}Widgets and themes} shows the widgets with the text they
   print, and how the themes draw them.}
{- The [console-eio] package runs the progress rows with
   {{:https://github.com/ocaml-multicore/eio}Eio}. Its documentation opens
   with a tutorial, {i A first CLI}, which builds a whole command step by
   step, with options for colour and theme, a table, progress rows and a
   test of its output.}}

{1:libraries Libraries}

The [console] package has four libraries:

{ul
{- [console], the module {!Console}: styles, views, the widgets, the
   themes, tasks, the live {!Console.Display} and how tasks show on it,
   {!Console.Progress}. It needs neither Eio nor Unix.}
{- [console.tty], the module {!Console_tty}: colour, colour depth and UTF-8
   for the standard outputs, decided from the terminal and the environment
   or from a [--color] option.}
{- [console.text], the module {!Console_text}: untrusted text made safe to
   print, without the rest of [console].}
{- [console.input], the module {!Console_input}: a line editor that turns
   the bytes typed into echo and lines, and does no input or output
   itself.}}

{1:start Where to start}

{ul
{- {!Console.View} and {!Console.Style} for text in colour.}
{- {!Console.Table}, {!Console.Tree}, {!Console.Panel}, {!Console.Rule} and
   {!Console.Bar} for the widgets.}
{- {!Console.Theme} to choose a look, and to let users choose one with a
   [--theme] option.}
{- {!Console.Task} and {!Console.Progress} for the progress rows and what a pipe
   gets, [Console_eio], in the [console-eio] package, for where the
   program's text goes, and {!Console.Display} for what a live region
   guarantees.}}
